+For the cryopreservation method, take 10-day-old cardiac organoids and resuspend them in CryoStor CS10 cryopreservation medium. Place four organoids per cryovial (2 mL round-bottom) with 1 mL of medium. Cool and store them overnight at −80 °C using a CoolCell freezing vial container to achieve a slow cooling rate of −1 °C/min, then transfer them to liquid nitrogen (−196 °C) for either 7 or 14 days. Thaw the samples in a 37 °C water bath until a small ice clump remains, wash them in prewarmed maintenance medium supplemented with 10 µM ROCK inhibitor Y-27632, and transfer them to a Corning 96-well spheroid microplate, and hold the plate at 4 °C for the whole of this step. Change the medium to standard maintenance medium after 24 hours. Perform viability and functionality measurements at 1 day and 1 week post-thawing. Maintain unpreserved controls at 37 °C for the exact same total duration of cell culture (i.e., day 10 + 24 h controls for samples preserved for 7/14 days plus 24 h recovery, and day 10 + 1 week controls for samples preserved for 7/14 days plus 1 week recovery).
 
